  "question": {
    "text": "There are two vessels filled with an ideal gas where volume of one is double the volume of other. The large vessel contains the gas at 8 kPa at 1000 K while the smaller vessel contains the gas at 7 kPa at 500 K. If the vessels are connected to each other by a thin tube allowing the gas to flow and the temperature of both vessels is maintained at 600 K , at steady state the pressure in the vessels will be (in kPa)."
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$4.4$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$6$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$24$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$18$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0013_e85de4423a2d.png\"/><br/>Number of masses will remain constant<br/>$\\begin{aligned}<br/>& \\mathrm{n}_1+\\mathrm{n}_2=\\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{f}} \\\\\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{P}_1 \\mathrm{~V}_1}{\\mathrm{RT}_1}+\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_2 \\mathrm{~V}_2}{\\mathrm{RT}_2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{f}} \\mathrm{~V}_{\\mathrm{f}}}{\\mathrm{RT}_{\\mathrm{f}}} \\\\\n& \\frac{8 \\times 2 \\mathrm{~V}}{\\mathrm{R} \\times 1000}+\\frac{7 \\times \\mathrm{V}}{\\mathrm{R} \\times 500}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{f}}(3 \\mathrm{~V})}{\\mathrm{R} \\times 600} \\\\\n& \\frac{16}{1000}+\\frac{14}{1000}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{f}}}{\\mathrm{R} \\times 600} \\\\\n& \\frac{30}{1000}=\\frac{\\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{f}}}{200} \\\\\n& \\mathrm{P}_{\\mathrm{f}}=6 \\mathrm{kPa}<br/>\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}